Changelog: 17-10-2026 12:45:18

Release 0.2.0.

Changelog: 17-10-2026 12:21:59

Fixed. The app's folder in the suite is apps/cec (was apps/hdmi-cec) and its package is hdmi_cec (was
bc250_hdmi_cec): the suite's naming convention (owner, 17-10-2026), a short folder name and the package named after
the app without its prefix; both names are the owner's. With the folder go its key in the portal, its chapter of
the wiki (apps/cec/, which the Manual links open), its installer test and its release tags: cec-v<x.y.z> from the
next release on, which the app's update check follows. The installed app keeps its name, its launcher
bc250-hdmi-cec, its folder under ~/.local/share, its settings, and the watcher and boot services under their names.
The watcher's unit names the package, so installing over an older copy points an existing unit at the new module,
with the jobs it had; the boot service in /etc runs its own copy of boot.py and is offered for an update in the app,
as for any change to that file. The portal moves its record of the installed copy to the new key.

